{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1773455264,"nonce":"yJsv1YhuYfQMqRiXAyEJ41IF68g=","message":"Implemented and validated on branch codex/history-resume-chat.\n\nChanges:\n- Added Resume live chat in History for Claude/Codex/Gemini entries by creating or reusing a console session bound to provider_session_id and navigating to Chat\n- History now injects the selected conversation into the sidebar if it is outside the current paged slice, so deep links from Chat still show the selected item\n- Added a shared selected-item auto-scroll hook and wired it into History, Issues, Inbox, and Auth sidebars\n- Replaced the Codex free-form-only picker with verified presets plus Custom fallback\n\nValidation:\n- Playwright: resumed a closed Claude history conversation into Chat and verified transcript hydration\n- Playwright: navigated Chat -\u003e View history and confirmed the selected history item was visible in the sidebar on clean load and on round-trip navigation\n- Playwright: resumed a Codex history conversation and verified the model picker shows default, gpt-5.2-codex, gpt-5.1-codex, gpt-5.1-codex-max, gpt-5-codex, and Custom…\n- Local CLI checks: gpt-5.2-codex, gpt-5.1-codex, gpt-5.1-codex-max, and gpt-5-codex all worked on this machine/account; codex-mini-latest was rejected for ChatGPT-account Codex CLI\n\nFindings:\n- The real reason the history sidebar still failed was not just missing scroll logic; the selected conversation could be absent from the initial 50-item slice, so there was nothing to scroll to until we explicitly pinned it into the rendered list\n- For validation, a fresh nonexistent MANDIBLE_DB path caused Mandible to copy a legacy DB into place, which can trigger unrelated startup collisions; pre-creating the DB file avoids that during isolated branch testing\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}